Author: Procr <193802945+procr1337@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 8 21:26:53 2026 +0000

    fix(warmup): actually run mHC tilelang warmup on NVIDIA GPUs
    
    The warmup was a complete no-op on NVIDIA because:
    
    1. _find_first_mhc_layer required hc_pre/hc_post attributes that only
       the AMD model's DeepseekV4DecoderLayer has. The nvidia model calls
       mhc_pre_tilelang/mhc_fused_post_pre_tilelang directly.
    
    2. Even if it had found the layer, it called layer.hc_pre() without
       norm_weight, compiling mhc_pre_big_fuse_tilelang. The nvidia
       forward pass always passes norm_weight, selecting the entirely
       different mhc_pre_big_fuse_with_norm_tilelang kernel.
    
    Fix _find_first_mhc_layer to check only the weight attributes common
    to all backends (hc_attn_fn, hc_attn_scale, etc.).
    
    Rewrite _warmup_layer_mhc to call mhc_pre_tilelang and
    mhc_fused_post_pre_tilelang directly with norm_weight, matching
    what the nvidia model forward() dispatches. This exercises all
    tilelang kernel variants: the with-norm big_fuse kernels across
    n_splits values, the fused-FMA kernel for small batches, and the
    post kernel.

